  "name": null,
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.20.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}",
